<title>AUSTRIA: DEHAENE SAYS 3 PCT DEFICIT GOAL KEY FOR EMU.</title>
<headline>DEHAENE SAYS 3 PCT DEFICIT GOAL KEY FOR EMU.</headline>
<dateline>SALZBURG, Austria 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Prime Minister Jean-Luc Dehaene told Reuters Financial Television on Thursday entrants into Europe's single currency would have to keep budget deficits as close as possible to the three percent criterion.</p>
<p>&quot;The objective is to be as near as possible to three percent and to be under three percent if possible,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Dehaene said delaying Europe's monetary union (EMU) beyond its planned starting date in January 1999 to give countries more time to get their deficits under control was not an option.</p>
<p>&quot;It is the worst option and it's an impossible option,&quot; he said. &quot;We have no other choice than to start on time.&quot;</p>
</text>
